00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:48.210
Fast Fact No.

326
00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:48.510
2.

327
00:12:48.510 --> 00:12:55.310
This episode originally aired in May of 2007 and it is a super-sized episode.

328
00:12:55.530 --> 00:12:55.790
Yes.

329
00:12:56.050 --> 00:13:00.390
However, when it re-ran in August, they cut it down.

330
00:13:00.950 --> 00:13:01.690
I know.

331
00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:03.290
They trimmed out a bunch of stuff.

332
00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:04.150
Why was that?

333
00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:10.870
The reason this was originally a super-sized episode is because this was our 50th episode of The Office.

334
00:13:11.150 --> 00:13:11.990
Oh, wow.

335
00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:14.390
So it was like a little celebration.

336
00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:19.090
But you know, then when shows re-run, they have to be regular size.

337
00:13:19.330 --> 00:13:20.010
Oh, I see.

338
00:13:20.450 --> 00:13:31.390
Well, to celebrate our 50th anniversary, we invited two super-fan Office bloggers to the set for a full day of filming so they could have a sneak peek.

339
00:13:31.570 --> 00:13:33.210
And do you remember who they were?

340
00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:38.390
Was it definitely Jenny Tan from Office Tally?

341
00:13:38.890 --> 00:13:39.490
Yes.

342
00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:42.050
And Kath Scary from Give Me My Remote.

343
00:13:42.290 --> 00:13:43.210
Oh, nice.

344
00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:45.450
Oh, they were so supportive of the show.

345
00:13:45.570 --> 00:13:52.690
I feel like they really were some of the first people organizing an online fan site where fans could go and share.

346
00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:53.790
Yeah.

347
00:13:53.990 --> 00:13:57.450
And the writers would read their sites and gather feedback.

348
00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:00.490
Like, they were a big part of formulating the show.

349
00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:02.950
I still go to officetally.com, Jenna.

350
00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:06.790
Like, when I'm looking up quotes when we're doing our podcast document and I'm like,

351
00:14:06.870 --> 00:14:12.530
oh, I want to get that exactly right, I will go to Office Tally because they usually have quotes up there.

352
00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:13.070
Yeah.

353
00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:23.410
Well, I went and looked at both of their blogs that they did after visiting the set, and I'm going to sprinkle in some of their observations as we go along in this episode.

354
00:14:23.570 --> 00:14:24.470
Oh, that's so fun.

355
00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:25.990
This is like a little time capsule.

356
00:14:26.230 --> 00:14:27.350
Yes, it was so cool.

357
00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:33.190
And by the way, okay, wait, here's one of the things that Jenny Tan wrote about her visit.

358
00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:34.650
This was just sort of an overview.

359
00:14:34.650 --> 00:14:35.070
Okay.

360
00:14:35.510 --> 00:14:38.530
She wrote, everybody works together really well.

361
00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:47.090
The actors are just incredible, and they are so well prepared, knew their lines, and I didn't hear any of them once ask for a line.

362
00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:48.950
That's true, though.

363
00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:49.810
That's true.

364
00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:51.570
We were pros.

365
00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:53.070
We came up ready to play.

366
00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:53.790
But you know what?

367
00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:55.090
Steve set the bar for that.

368
00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:56.330
We've said that many times.

369
00:14:57.230 --> 00:15:04.230
She also probably couldn't see that we had our scripts hidden in our desks, and we would sometimes have to sneak a look.

370
00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:06.310
We had to sneak a look between takes.

371
00:15:06.730 --> 00:15:07.450
We did do that.

372
00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:10.010
We did sort of like just look over them really quickly.

373
00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:11.230
But that's all right.

374
00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:12.370
That's all right.

375
00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:15.410
We were never like, line, can I get my line?

